 Alain Tremblay launches his second album, 'Le poids des papillons'

 After more than a year of work, Alain Tremblay finally presents his second
 album, "Le poids des papillons", a collection of twelve authentic tracks that
 took flight across streaming platforms on April 22. Entrusted to the expert
 care of producer Guy Tourville, this new offering reveals a brighter, more
 introspective side of the artist from L'Isle-aux-Coudres.

 "I took advantage of the pandemic to work heavily on the lyrics and the
 music", shares the singer-songwriter. "This album is much more deeply attached
 to the realities of life and my personal perceptions on certain subjects, such
 as protecting the planet. I also speak about the vital importance of the
 French language. We must act and reflect on what we want to leave behind for
 the generation that is coming next."

